# Database — PostgreSQL

## General

- PostgreSQL only; migrations via **Flyway** (`V{n}__description.sql`).
- ACID transactions required for points/bids; consider Redis for ephemeral auction timer state (sync to Postgres on close).

## JSONB usage

- `audit_log.payload` — flexible audit data per `AuditLogType`.
- `item_weapon.special_effects`, `item_armor.special_effects`, `item_accessory.special_effects` — arrays up to 4 effects.

## Item modeling (1:1 extension)

- Base `item` (type, name, rarity, image_url, …).
- Type tables: `item_weapon`, `item_armor`, `item_accessory`, `item_misc`.
- Upgrades: `item_talic` (item_id, talic_type, level 0–7, slot); `UNIQUE (item_id, talic_type)`.

## Key indexes & constraints

- `idx_event_claim_daily` on `(member_id, objective_id, claimed_date)` — LIMITADO daily cap (`claimed_date` generated column UTC).
- `idx_single_leader` partial unique on `member(role)` WHERE `LIDER`.
- `UNIQUE (event_id, member_id)` on `event_claim` — one claim per event.
- `idx_auction_bid_auction` on `(auction_id, amount DESC, created_at DESC)`.
- Check constraints for enums: role, status, objective type, item type, auction status.

New migrations: additive preferred; never edit applied Flyway files.
